@startuml campusclaw_actuator_boundary
' Source evidence: campusclaw/src/main/resources/application.properties:1-23 at b46b9d37e634dae12a777576062e2097516fe153.
' Source evidence: campusclaw/pom.xml does not directly declare Actuator at the same baseline.
' User-provided target condition: CampusClaw is deployed as a standalone company service.
' Observed behavior: the baseline application disabled management access and excluded Actuator auto-configurations.
' Architecture change: the standalone service no longer overrides Actuator behavior in application properties.
' Design reason: the company runtime boundary owns management policy for the standalone service.

title CampusClaw Standalone Actuator Configuration Boundary

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

cloud "Company runtime platform" as platform
artifact "NativeParent and runtime policy" as policy
component "CampusClaw standalone service" as service
file "application.properties\nbusiness configuration only" as application
component "Optional Actuator runtime" as actuator

platform --> service : deploy and configure
policy --> service : build and runtime defaults
application --> service : server, database, CampusMate, logging
service --> actuator : uses when present

note right of application
  No management.* overrides.
  No Actuator auto-configuration exclusions.
end note

note bottom of actuator
  Presence, port, and exposure follow
  the effective company runtime policy.
end note
@enduml
